I'd like to start building planning/plan.md in its step order, 1 step at a time. For each step, can we first write and test the plan names, run it and show it failing, then stop; after we commit the failing test (`Test first: <step>`), write the code until it passes, then
     stop again so we commit it (`Step <n>: <step>`);every test uses mock responses saved under `tests/mock_responses/`, and no test calls the real
     model or reads `API_KEY`;
   - the expected values in each test are the expected facts of the test plan, not values copied
     from a run;
   - after each step, run the whole test suite and stop if anything fails.

